## 2. Factory: one `ReceiverOptions` **per member**, with unique IDs

Each member needs its own `client.id` (for metrics/logs) and — if you use static membership — its own **unique** `group.instance.id`. Two members with the same `group.instance.id` fence each other out, and you'd see exactly the "1 member" symptom.

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class ReceiverOptionsFactory {

    private final KafkaProperties bootProps;
    private final AppProperties app;
    private final InstanceIdentity identity;     // stable per pod, see §4

    public ResolvedConsumer resolve(TopicHandler<?> handler) {
        var o = app.consumerFor(handler.topic());

        String groupId   = o != null && o.groupId() != null ? o.groupId() : handler.consumerGroup();
        int concurrency  = o != null && o.partitionConcurrency() != null ? o.partitionConcurrency() : app.kafka().defaultPartitionConcurrency();
        int count        = o != null && o.consumerCount() != null ? o.consumerCount() : handler.consumerCount();
        boolean enabled  = o == null || o.isEnabled();

        Map<String, Object> base = new HashMap<>(bootProps.buildConsumerProperties());
        base.putAll(handler.consumerOverrides());
        if (o != null && o.properties() != null) base.putAll(o.properties());
        base.put(ConsumerConfig.GROUP_ID_CONFIG, groupId);
        base.put(ConsumerConfig.ENABLE_AUTO_COMMIT_CONFIG, false);
        base.put(ConsumerConfig.KEY_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, StringDeserializer.class);
        base.put(ConsumerConfig.VALUE_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, ByteArrayDeserializer.class);
        base.put(ConsumerConfig.PARTITION_ASSIGNMENT_STRATEGY_CONFIG, CooperativeStickyAssignor.class.getName());

        List<ReceiverOptions<String, byte[]>> members = new ArrayList<>(count);
        for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
            Map<String, Object> cfg = new HashMap<>(base);
            String memberId = groupId + "-" + identity.id() + "-" + i;         // unique per member
            cfg.put(ConsumerConfig.CLIENT_ID_CONFIG, memberId);
            if (identity.isStable()) {                                          // StatefulSet / fixed hostnames only
                cfg.put(ConsumerConfig.GROUP_INSTANCE_ID_CONFIG, memberId);
            }
            members.add(ReceiverOptions.<String, byte[]>create(cfg)
                    .subscription(List.of(handler.topic()))
                    .commitInterval(Duration.ofMillis(200))
                    .commitBatchSize(10)
                    .maxDeferredCommits(concurrency * 10)
                    .addAssignListener(p -> log.info("[{}] assigned {}", memberId, p))
                    .addRevokeListener(p -> log.info("[{}] revoked {}", memberId, p)));
        }
        return new ResolvedConsumer(handler.topic(), groupId, concurrency, enabled, members);
    }

    public record ResolvedConsumer(String topic, String groupId, int concurrency, boolean enabled,
                                   List<ReceiverOptions<String, byte[]>> members) {}
}
```

