## 4. Stable identity for static membership

```java
@Component
public class InstanceIdentity {
    private final String id;
    private final boolean stable;

    public InstanceIdentity(@Value("${app.instance-id:}") String configured) {
        if (!configured.isBlank()) { id = configured; stable = true; }          // e.g. from StatefulSet ordinal
        else { id = UUID.randomUUID().toString().substring(0, 8); stable = false; }
    }
    public String id() { return id; }
    public boolean isStable() { return stable; }
}
```

```yaml
# k8s StatefulSet – pod name is national-code-checker-0, -1, -2 …
env:
  - name: APP_INSTANCE_ID
    valueFrom: { fieldRef: { fieldPath: metadata.name } }
```

Rule: **`group.instance.id` only when the identity survives restarts**. For a plain Deployment or local runs, leave it off (random `client.id` only) — otherwise every restart with a *different* id keeps the old, dead member in the group until `session.timeout.ms`, and two pods that accidentally share an id fence each other.

